<title>GREECE: PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) CUTS GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES.</title>
<headline>PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) CUTS GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek gasoline prices (including VAT) will be slashed by 2.80 drachmas per litre and transport diesel by 2.20 drachmas, effective on Thursday and for one week, the Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) said in a statement.</p>
<p>The price of diesel used as heating fuel will go down by 2.70 drachmas per litre.</p>
<p>The price adjustments come after lower world gasoline prices, down by $12.4 per metric tonne, lower diesel prices, down by $8.6 for transport and $10.5 for heating and a lower dollar/drachma exchange rate. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
